ke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/></svg></button></div></div></div></section>
<section data-name="Symbol + Text" data-node-id="750:970" data-role="introduction" data-tone="white"><div data-part="artwork" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{base}/media/c637e0d8e458864a395d.svg" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div data-part="copy"><p data-part="paragraph" class="display-prose">The Vessyl is a hotel in Arenal, Costa Rica, built around a dome made for sound. Fourteen units sit apart from one another across the property, so getting from your bed to dinner is a walk through forest rather than a hallway.</p>
<p data-part="paragraph" class="display-prose">There is a river you can swim in, horses, a kitchen that changes its menu every day, and a founder who lives here. Some people come for three nights and never leave the land. Some drive up for one session in the Dome and go back to their hotel in town. Both are the right way to do this.</p></div></section>
<section data-name="Section - 40/60 text image" data-node-id="857:15228" data-role="split" data-layout="copy-first" data-variant="editorial"><div data-part="copy"><p data-node-id="I857:15228;748:584;748:551" data-part="eyebrow">STAY WITH US</p>
<h2 data-node-id="I857:15228;748:584;748:552" class="c-heading" data-part="heading">Fourteen units,{' '}no two the same</h2>
<p data-part="paragraph">Six villas, one treehouse and seven glamping tents, placed so that each one faces something different. Choose by the view, by how much privacy you want, and by how far you feel like walking to dinner. The treehouse books out first, every season.</p>
<div data-part="actions"><a data-name="CTA" data-node-id="I857:15228;748:584;750:1289;750:1257" class="current-action" data-part="action" href="{base}/{edition}/where-you-sleep/">SEE WHERE YOU WILL SLEEP</a></div></div>
